SYNTHESIS
========================================================================================================================
1. Rank gauges are useful diagnostics but poor tournaments: H usually collapses to 1.
2. Phase/open-arc gauges are global circular-spread meters; phase_H is the HYP-1970 channel.
3. Close/danger/kinetic-close switches preserve local 1/n crowding and approach bits.
4. Blocker, two-neighbor, and threshold-deficit relief are pressure gauges; SCC > 1 is the core alarm.
5. Observer-two-guard is the marked loneliness channel: observer outdegree tracks the bracket directly.
6. Runner-level endpoint summaries were transitive here; endpoint data should stay labelled, not collapsed.
7. A useful LRC metric is therefore a bundle:
   phase_H + open_arc scores + threshold-switch c3 + pressure SCC/sinks + observer out + endpoint debt.
